        "The first model is a custom Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) to classify brain MRI images into four tumor categories. The model included multiple convolutional and pooling layers for feature extraction, followed by dropout and dense layers for classification. I used categorical_crossentropy as the loss function and the Adam optimizer. During training, both training and validation accuracies steadily increased, and the losses decreased without major divergence, indicating stable learning.\n",
