    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For the second model, I have implemented Transfer Learning using MobileNetV2, a pre-trained convolutional neural network originally trained on the ImageNet dataset. I used MobileNetV2 as a fixed feature extractor by freezing its base layers and adding custom dense layers on top for classifying brain tumor images. This allowed me to leverage powerful, pre-learned visual features while only training the final classifier layers on my dataset. The model was compiled using the Adam optimizer with a low learning rate and trained for 25 epochs with early stopping and checkpoint callbacks.\n",
        "\n",
        "The MobileNetV2 model outperformed the custom CNN, achieving a test accuracy of 86.18% , which was the highest so far. The training and validation curves showed smooth and steady improvements without overfitting. It generalized well to unseen data, and the accuracy/loss graphs confirmed that the model was learning effectively."
      ],
