    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### 1. Which Evaluation metrics did you consider for a positive business impact and why?\n",
        "\n",
        "---"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "h_CCil-SKHpo"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For this project, I mainly used accuracy as the evaluation metric. Accuracy tells how many times the model gave the correct prediction, and since this is a medical project, it’s important that the model is correct most of the time.\n",
        "\n",
        "But in real-world situations like hospitals, just accuracy is not enough. We also need to look at precision and recall. Precision makes sure we don’t wrongly say a person has a tumor when they don’t, and recall makes sure we don’t miss any actual tumor cases. So both are important when dealing with health data.\n",
        "\n",
        "Even though I focused on accuracy while training, I now understand that using precision, recall, and F1-score gives a better picture of the model’s real-world performance and can help avoid serious medical mistakes."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "jHVz9hHDKFms"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
